hypotheses.statement:
Over every field and for every integer $m\geq0$, $$\label{eq:cw-power-rank}
 \operatorname{R}(\mathrm{CW}_q^{\otimes m})
      \leq(q+2)^m\binom{3m+2}{2}.$$

For fixed population data, there is a function $\xi(\eta,\chi)\to0$ as $(\eta,\chi)\to(0,0)$ such that any fine side variable passing the pair filters is compatible with at most $$\label{eq:compatibility-degree}
 \exp\bigl(N(A_{\rm amb}-C_W+\xi(\eta,\chi))
                    +O(\log N)\bigr),\qquad W\in\{Y,Z\},$$ target triples containing its coarse block, before hashing. The estimate is uniform in the variable and the target arrangement.

The exact parameters above satisfy every positivity and balance condition used in Proposition <a href="#prop:staggered-yield" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="prop:staggered-yield">10</a>. All thirty partial capacity entries in Table <a href="#tab:capacities" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="tab:capacities">1</a> are positive. In particular, $S_*>0$, $T\log2-B_*>0$, all entries of $L_A,L_B,L_C$ are positive, and the three balance fractions are strictly positive. Moreover, $$\begin{aligned}
 5.612983956059236756&<H_0+C_*<5.612983956059236757,\label{eq:yield-certificate}\\
 12.594770321594676362&<S_*<12.594770321594676363,\label{eq:volume-certificate}\\
 2.371054886006745684
 &<\frac{3(8\log7-H_0-C_*)}{S_*}
       <2.371054886006745685.\label{eq:ratio-certificate}
\end{aligned}$$ With $\Omega=2.371056$, the strict comparison has the outward enclosure $$\label{eq:gap-certificate}
 0.000004676829725968
 < H_0+C_*+\frac{\Omega}{3}S_*-8\log7
 <0.000004676829725969.$$

